    "commit_body": "Vol-fair score-stage dampener that lifts put scores OUT of any put bucket\n(<=25) when the underlying recently fell more than 1.0 stock-sigmas over\nthe last 10 trading bars. Eliminates the put-cohort regression where puts\nfiring immediately after sharp drops underperform the put baseline by\n-7.15pp WR15 at the option-aligned barrier (z=-6.88, N=2,767 over 5y).\n\nMechanism (in compute_overall_score, applied AFTER continuation boost,\nBEFORE earnings boost so the boost can't re-amplify a displaced peak):\n\n    if overall <= 25 and ret_10d_sigma <= -1.0:\n        overall = max(overall, 30)\n\nret_10d_sigma = ret_10d / (sigma_60 * sqrt(10)), where sigma_60 is the\n60-day realized daily stdev \u2014 same vol definition the strategy's TP/SL\nbarriers use. Sigma-normalization corrects the stock-vol confound: a -10%\nmove is a 3sigma crash for low-vol KO but normal noise for high-vol PLTR;\nthe cohort regression is concentrated in low/mid-vol stocks (z=-5.03 vs\nz=-1.63 for high-vol). Sigma cutoff applies the same crash semantics\nacross all stocks regardless of base volatility.\n\nPer-trade ship gate H1-H5 (5y, option-aligned barrier 30dte_opt at W=15d):\n  H1: <5 +2.95pp / <15 +3.22pp / <25 +1.56pp WR15 lift\n  H2: WR15/WR30 directional consistency\n  H3: ~30% of <=25 peaks displaced (designed; v27 WCF precedent dropped 75%);\n      absolute floor N>>50 on every primary tier\n  H4: puts strictly improved (this is the cohort suppression)\n  H5: sign-consistent across 1y/3y/5y on all three put tiers\n  Calls: 95+/90+/85+/80+/75+/70+ all unchanged (gate is overall<=25)\n\nPlumbing: build_ret10d_sigma_map() joins per-symbol price history to a\n{date: ret_10d_sigma} map at the start of each batch scorer (calculate_,\nrecalculate_scores_batched + simulator). Score.calculate_overall_score\nsingle-row path does a lightweight 80-bar lookback when called outside\nthe batch context.\n\nNo portfolio params changed. No drift-guard impact (PCD lives in\nscoring.py, not strategy_config.py). Investigation artifacts in\nexperiments/post_crash_v2/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
